                <pb facs="0380" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg300"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Iddings.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 81, of August 29
                    last, I have to say that the Department will be pleased to have you send to it
                    three copies of the recent Italian convention with the Sultan of Somaliland as
                    soon as it shall have been published by the Italian Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
